<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsering Dondub</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsering Dondub was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> commander under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsewang-rabtan">Tsewang Rabtan</a>. In 1717 he led an army across the Tibetan plateau, killed the Khoshut ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhazang-khan">Lha-bzang Khan</a> and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a>, and in 1718 his forces destroyed a Qing relief army near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salween">Salween</a> River. A second Qing expedition drove the Dzungars from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> in 1720, beginning Qing supervision of Tibet. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dawachi">Dawachi</a> became the last Dzungar khan.</p></div>
